<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/815189530%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Arch of Marcus Antonius";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432695%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called \"Arch of Marcus Antonius\" takes its name from a local tradition that the citizens of Aquinum built the monument in a single day to honor Antonius. In all likelihood, it is a monument connected either to a deductio of veterans sent to Aquinum in 41 BCE or to the work of Caius Calvisius Sabinus who reorganized the via Latina in 27 BCE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/815189530> .

