<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/821658053%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Clivus Suburanus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/208084575%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/29110684%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/557607129%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Clivus Suburanus was a street of the ancient city of Rome. It rose from the Oppian and Cispian Hills and continued to the Porta Esquilina. Some current urban streets - via in Selci, via di San Martino, and via di S. Vito - approximate at least part of its course.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/821658053> .

