    rdfs:label "Temple of Ellesyia";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/795845%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A small rock-cut temple dedicated to Amun, Horus, and Satis dated to the 18th Dynasty. Originally located near Qasr Ibrim/Premis, the temple was relocated to the Museo Egizio in Turin, Italy, in the 1960s prior to the area's flooding beneath the surface of Lake Nasser.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/837295553> .

