<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/840019989%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Stoa at Brauron";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/579879%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Stoa at Brauron, within the larger Artemis Brauronia complex, housed dining spaces as well as votive offerings to the goddess Artemis. The Stoa was Π-shaped, wrapping around a courtyard that separated it from the temple of Artemis at Brauron, which it faced. Worship at the cult site began ca. the eighth century BCE. The site was abandoned after a flood in the third century BCE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/840019989> .

