<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/841475483%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Palatium Sessorianum";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/18528486%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Palatium Sessorianum is of unknown origins. It was situated at the extreme south-east of Region V and it adjoined the amphitheatrum Castrense. It pre-dated the Aurelian wall. The portions of the complex within the line of the walls was an imperial residence by the time of Constantine.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/841475483> .

