    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/694134032%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Aedicula Concordia was a bronze shrine of Concord located on the Graecostasis in Rome. Cn. Flavius erected it when he was aedile in 304 B.C. It is presumed to have been destroyed when the later Temple of Concord was dedicated in 121 B.C.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/844972184> .

