<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/862544795%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Tell el-ʻAbd";
    rdfs:comment "Mound site along the eastern bank of the Euphrates in northern Syria. The site shows signs of habitation from the Early Bronze Age through the Byzantine period. Tell el-ʻAbd was flooded by the construction of the Taqba Dam in 1975, though a portion of it has reemerged due to declining water levels in Lake Assad.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/862544795> .

