<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/862707560%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Değirmenköy";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/214160492%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Değirmenköy is a modern Turkish settlement with an Urartian fortress situated nearby. Here, a cylindrical stone with an inscription of the Urartian king Minua, son of Išpuini (9th / 8th century BCE) has been found mentioning a \"barzudibiduni building of Minua\" (CTU A 5-64).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/862707560> .

