    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/978527351%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Major burial ground of the late Bronze Age Koban culture, which flourished in the Caucasus from ca. 1400-400 BCE. The Tli necropolis, named after the nearby modern village of Tli, contains 481 graves dated from the Middle Bronze Age through the Iron Age.";
