        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/679976755%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An early Imperial building on the Esquiline Hill in Rome, the Auditorium Maecenatis has been connected with Maecenas as it stands in the area of his gardens (horti). While its precise function is unknown, the building may have served as a conservatory.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/866548110> .

