    rdfs:label "Grand Lagneux Roman Bath";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/167759%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "At Grand Lagneux, a small village in the French commune of Yenne, a rescue excavation in 2020 revealed part of a Roman-era bathing establishment. The excavated site is now buried under a modern home. This find constitutes another possible locality in the commune for attested ancient name \"Etanna\".";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/867265469> .

