<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/868835070%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "House of Thiasus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/680072866%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A domus at Pompeii located on Via Nola in insula 10 of Regio IX. Partial excavation at the site occurred in 1888; scientific excavations resumed in 2023. Epigraphic evidence suggests that one of the domus' owners was connected to the duovir Aulus Rustius Verus. In February 2025, a mid-first-century BCE room with a painted Dionysiac cycle was discovered.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/868835070> .

