<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874397%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Batas-Harir";
    rdfs:comment "A first-century CE rock-cut relief at Batas-Harir is likely associated with the Parthian culture and depicts a ruler, perhaps the king Abdissares or Izates II or III of Adiabene. The site is located in Iraqi Kurdistan in the Erbil Governorate.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874397> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874397/osm-location-of-batas-harir-relief> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
