<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874800%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Zernaki tepe";
    rdfs:comment "An ancient place in Van province, Turkey. It had a street grid, fortifications of mud brick on a polygonal masonry foundation, and at least 14 building inscriptions in Aramaic from the Parthian period. Professor Rafet Çavuşoğlu began a program of excavations in 2021, which appears to be unpublished as of October 2025.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874800> .

