<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/88092816%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Pincian Hill";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Pincian Hill in Rome likely takes its name from the Pincii, an ancient family. It is not considered a member of the canonical grouping of Rome's hills, but it did lie within the line of the walls built by Aurelian. In the early Imperial period, it is known as a zone of elaborate gardens, hence the moniker \"collis hortulorum\".";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/88092816> .

