    rdfs:label "Ziwiye";
    rdfs:comment "Ziwiye is the name of a modern village in northwestern Iran. It is associated with an archaeological site from the 7th century BCE that was looted in the mid-20th century and subsequently partially excavated in a more scientific manner. The site's ancient name is not known.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/884230> .

