<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/89102%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Watercrook Roman Fort and Settlement";
    rdfs:comment "The Roman Fort near Watercrook Farm (at Kendal in northwest England) was originally built ca. AD 90 and rebuilt ca. AD 130. It may have been called Alone?/Alauna? in antiquity. Its poorly preserved remains are coincident with those of a contemporaneous civilian settlement.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/89102> .

