    rdfs:label "Langton";
    rdfs:comment "Multiple phases of a Romano-British villa were excavated at Langton, East Riding, Yorkshire, England. The site was discovered in 1899 and excavations took place in 1926 and 1930-31. The original phase of the site might have been either a military outpost or an indigenous farmstead.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/89223> .

