<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/894058%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Paikuli";
    rdfs:comment "At Paikuli, located in what is now the southern part of Iraqi Kurdistan near the modern-day village of Barkal, Sulaymaniyah Governorate, Iraq, are the remains of a stone masonry tower that was erected as a monument to a victory enjoyed by the Sasanian emperor Narseh over his grandnephew. The inscription is now housed in the Sulaymaniyah Museum.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/894058> .

