<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/896005683%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Schola Xanthi";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/152699900%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Schola Xanthi was likely the seat of the scribae, praecones, and librarii of the curule aediles. A dedicatory inscription names Bebryx Aug. lib. Drusianus and A. Fabius Xanthus as those responsible for erecting the structure during the principate of Tiberius. There was a subsequent renovation in the third century. The Schola Xanthi is thought to correspond with a structure excavated in 1539 on the clivus Capitolinus between the Arch of Septimius Severus and the Arch of Tiberius. The archaeological remains do not survive.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/896005683> .

