<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/897836%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Rumakan";
    rdfs:comment "An ancient settlement or region of Babylonia whose precise location cannot be determined today. It was established as a tax-collection sub-district of Vēh-Artakhshatr by Ardashīr I. This place was also called Rumae and is referred to in the Babylonian Talmud, Treatise Megillah 26b, as having had a Jewish community.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/897836> .

