<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/801400483%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Bath F3";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/181763748%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/356665990%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893990%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Bath building originally occupying all of Block F3, located in the intramuros military sector of Dura-Europos. Excavations reveal that the bath likely had two phases of renovation (one perhaps after 165 CE, and another around c. 200 CE), before it was destroyed by fire. Dura-Europos' amphitheater was built over the remains of Bath F3, and thus the amphitheater's dedicatory inscription, dated to 216 CE, serves as a terminus ante quem for the bath building.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/801400483> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/801408827> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
