<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/815189530> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Arachne sog. Bogen des Marcus Antonius Aquino, (Aquinum), Frosinone (Provinz)",
        "De Maria 1988 pp. 53, 231",
        "Wikidata Arch of Mark Antony (Q3621781)",
        "Wikipedia (Italian) Arco di Marcantonio",
        "vici.org 29247: Aquinum, Arch of Mark Antony";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The so-called \"Arch of Marcus Antonius\" takes its name from a local tradition that the citizens of Aquinum built the monument in a single day to honor Antonius. In all likelihood, it is a monument connected either to a deductio of veterans sent to Aquinum in 41 BCE or to the work of Caius Calvisius Sabinus who reorganized the via Latina in 27 BCE.";
    dcterms:modified "2026-01-18T15:57:06-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Arch of Marcus Antonius";
    cito:citesAsRelated <https://arachne.dainst.org/entity/5773>,
