    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/857018%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A number of monumental, rupestral tombs at ancient Amaseia (modern Amasya in Turkey) among which 5 large ones are mentioned by Strabo and attributed to the kings. Mount Harşena and the Rock-tombs of the Pontic Kings were submitted to the Tentative World Heritage Lists in 2005 by the Permanent Delegation of Turkey to UNESCO.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/825080162> .

