    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Une grande villa antique à Auxerre (Yonne) ",
        "Villa baths brought to light in Auxerre, France ";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "Located 3 km south of the town of Auxerre, France, on the right bank of the Yonne River, archaeologists excavated the remains of an extensive Gallo-Roman villa covering an area of approximately 1.6 hectares. The villa site includes a bath complex. The site has been noted for its archaeological potential since the nineteenth century. While some excavations took place in the 1960s, the open-area excavation of the villa was announced in 2025.";
    dcterms:modified "2025-06-25T11:55:22-04:00";
    dcterms:title "ville d’Auxerre";
    cito:citesForInformation <https://ancientbaths.com/2025/06/25/villa-baths-brought-to-light-in-auxerre-france/>,
        <https://www.inrap.fr/une-grande-villa-antique-auxerre-yonne-20067>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/138206>;
