        "vici.org 36049: Mazara del Vallo, Hypogeum of St. Bartholomew";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "A system of caves located in Mazara del Vallo, Sicily, on the right bank of the Mazaro River. Human occupation of the caves began with the Diana Culture (ca. 3500 BCE) and continued into modernity. A paleochristian catacomb was also identified here in the 19th century.";
