<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/856859068%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ehilikalamma";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/33309869%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/54136920%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/568355929%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893951%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The temple of the goddess Ašratu, Ehilikalamma (“House of the Luxuriance of the Land”), was located in the Ka-dingirra district (modern Sahn) of Babylon. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, this was one of four temples in that part of the city, which was located in the northern part of the eastern half of Babylon.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/856859068> .

