<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/868586791%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Assur Archive 42";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893945%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "In a house in cD9II, built against the outside of the then-ruined inner town wall, excavators discovered an archive of 22 clay tablets and envelopes, 3 of them written in Aramaic. The texts date to the 7th century BCE. The archive, belonging Aššur-šallim-aḫḫe and others, consisted of loan documents, and other material, such as a juridical document, a letter, and a lump of clay with a seal impression.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/868586791> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/868835070> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Barbella 2025 ",
        "Benforte 2025 ",
        "POMPEII, DISCOVERY OF A ROOM WITH FRESCOES DEPICTING THE INITIATION INTO THE MYSTERIES AND THE DIONYSIAC PROCESSION ",
        "Wikidata House of Thiasus (Q133270544)",
        "Wikimedia Commons Category:House of Thiasus",
        "Wikipedia (English) House of Thiasus",
        "vici.org 103598";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "A domus at Pompeii located on Via Nola in insula 10 of Regio IX. Partial excavation at the site occurred in 1888; scientific excavations resumed in 2023. Epigraphic evidence suggests that one of the domus' owners was connected to the duovir Aulus Rustius Verus. In February 2025, a mid-first-century BCE room with a painted Dionysiac cycle was discovered.";
    dcterms:modified "2026-07-05T19:00:05-04:00";
    dcterms:title "House of Thiasus";
    cito:citesAsRelated <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:House_of_Thiasus>,
        <https://vici.org/vici/103598/>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q133270544>;
    cito:citesForInformation <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Thiasus>,
        <https://pompeiisites.org/e-journal-degli-scavi-di-pompei/la-casa-come-palcoscenico-il-complesso-termale-e-conviviale-recentemente-scoperto-nellinsula-ix-10-a-pompei/>,
        <https://pompeiisites.org/e-journal-degli-scavi-di-pompei/lo-sguardo-della-baccante-la-nuova-megalografia-di-ii-stile-a-tema-dionisiaco-nella-casa-del-tiaso-ix-10-3-a-pompei/>,
