    dcterms:coverage "Paikuli";
    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/39678158>,
        <http://viaf.org/viaf/52023947>;
    dcterms:description "At Paikuli, located in what is now the southern part of Iraqi Kurdistan near the modern-day village of Barkal, Sulaymaniyah Governorate, Iraq, are the remains of a stone masonry tower that was erected as a monument to a victory enjoyed by the Sasanian emperor Narseh over his grandnephew. The inscription is now housed in the Sulaymaniyah Museum.";
