    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "CIL VI, 103 = 30692",
        "Gorski and Packer 2015 no. 16 - The Schola Xanthi",
        "Platner 1929 (Perseus) SCHOLA XANTHI",
        "Wikidata Schola Xanthi (Q130506371)";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The Schola Xanthi was likely the seat of the scribae, praecones, and librarii of the curule aediles. A dedicatory inscription names Bebryx Aug. lib. Drusianus and A. Fabius Xanthus as those responsible for erecting the structure during the principate of Tiberius. There was a subsequent renovation in the third century. The Schola Xanthi is thought to correspond with a structure excavated in 1539 on the clivus Capitolinus between the Arch of Septimius Severus and the Arch of Tiberius. The archaeological remains do not survive.";
    dcterms:modified "2025-01-12T09:19:23-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Schola Xanthi";
    cito:citesAsEvidence <https://www.zotero.org/groups/pleiades/items/JCY8WN8B>;
