    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Bouchon 2014 pages 483-486",
        "CFL/AGO Report 4726: KASTRI LIVADIOU. - Ancienne Dolichè - 2008",
        "CFL/AGO Toponyme 32847: Livadion",
        "ToposText Kastri Livadiou (Larisa) Dolichi",
        "Wikidata Kastri Dolichis (Q16327156)",
        "Wikipedia (Greek) Αρχαιολογικός χώρος “Καστρί” Δολίχης",
        "iDAI.gazetteer 2361868: Kastri Livadiou",
        "vici.org 32352: Kastri",
        "Αρχαιολογικός Χώρος Δολίχης (Περραιβια blog) ";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:description "An archaeological site located 4.5km west southwest of modern Dolichi in Greece's Larisa regional unit (Thessaly). Here, a proto-byzantine walled settlement with three basilicas was built partly with spolia from a temple of Herakles and the ancient city of Doliche. On this basis, the excavators have argued for identification of the archaeology with the attested name; however, the lack so far of in-situ evidence predating the 6th century CE has led other scholars to continue to identify the original Classical-Roman polis of Doliche with the archaeological site at Sarandoporo.";
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-18T13:20:13-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Kastri Livadiou ancient settlement";
