    rdfs:comment "Nineveh’s outer stone wall was called Badnigerimhuluha (\"Wall, Terrorizer of Enemies\"). It was constructed by the Neo-Assyrian king Sennacherib after he moved the Assyrian capital to Nineveh. The visible remains of the twelve-kilometer-long wall and some of its gates are still visible today.";
